# ── (#R257) Claude Code のローカル上書き ─────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md（追跡対象）は恒久指示。CLAUDE.local.md はこのマシン固有の情報と
# 資格情報を持つ。このリポジトリは public なので、絶対に追跡してはならない。
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── GPT ↔ Claude handoff workspace ───────────────────────────────────────────
# ChatGPT Work edits the single local HANDOFF.md in this folder. The bridge
# keeps it deliberately outside Git so evolving prompts and approvals never
# become source-code dirt or leak into parallel Claude worktrees.
GPT-HANDOFF/

# ── Ops / test tooling (added R133) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev/test dependencies and their build artifacts. The IntMap app itself ships
# NO node_modules — these exist only for CI and local testing.
node_modules/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/
npm-debug.log*
*.local.env
.env

# ── Supabase local dev + DB backups (added R134) ─────────────────────────────
# CLI local state (link info, downloaded CLI). config.toml/migrations/seed ARE tracked.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.env
supabase/functions/**/.env
# DB dumps / encrypted backups must NEVER be committed to this public repo.
/backups/
*.dump
*.dump.gpg
*.sql.gpg


# ── Vite build output (added R175) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run build` emits the deployable tree here; GitHub Pages publishes it from CI.
dist/
dist-dev/

# ── (#R209) the frame instrument's tile replay cache ─────────────────────────
# scripts/frame-profile.mjs answers every external request from here so an A/B
# compares identical bytes. Recorded third-party tiles — never committed.
.frame-cache/

# (#R243) round scratch — screenshots and one-off probes, never shipped
/x/

# ── (#R262) build caches for the shipped earth-structure rasters ─────────────
# scripts/build-vs30.mjs keeps 8,089 terrarium tiles here; build-slab2/crust1/
# tectonics keep their upstream downloads. All are re-fetchable, none ship.
.cache/
__pycache__/

# ── (#R311) the build report the perf gate reads ─────────────────────────────
# vite writes .perf/build-report.json on every build: it describes ONE build
# (which chunks are eager, what each costs raw/gzip/brotli), not the repository.
# The committed side is tests/perf-baseline.json — the numbers the gate ratchets.
.perf/

# ── (#R338) the preview config is MACHINE-LOCAL, not shared ──────────────────
# .claude/launch.json holds absolute paths into this machine's worktrees
# (C:/Users/.../Temp/intmap-worktrees/wt-r330/dist). Nothing outside this
# machine can use them, and tracking them cost something real: the preview tool
# writes into the MASTER's copy, so while any concurrent session had a preview
# open the master's fast-forward was refused — correctly, because §6 forbids
# touching another session's uncommitted work — and with it the USB backup
# (`skipped master-not-synced`). MEASURED at #R334: 19 sessions running at once,
# the master 3 commits behind, the backup skipped. Untracked, the file is still
# written and still read (scripts/worktree.mjs derives the free round number
# from it); it just stops standing in the way of everyone else's merge.
.claude/launch.json
.cache/
